            <ArticleTitle>Coronary Artery Pseudoaneurysm due to Medial Mucoid Degeneration Mimicking an Intra-atrial Mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2453-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2169/internalmedicine.54.3804</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysms are frequently asymptomatic and may be difficult to diagnose by cardiac imaging. We herein present a case of a coronary artery aneurysm of the right coronary artery due to medial mucoid degeneration mimicking an intra-atrial mass on echocardiography and magnetic resonance imaging, with the cause being diagnosed after surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
